      "id": 8287,
      "name": "Matchstickman",
      "username": "Matchstickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-07-03T07:24:21.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So last night we played a game via G+ against the Matriarch, we didn't win, despite our valiant attempt but we did learn an interesting thing.</p><p>Team Leader Tachyon's incapacitated powers are</p><ul>\n<li>One Player draws 1 card now</li>\n<li><span>One Player plays 1 card now</span></li>\n<li><span>Shuffle a trash into its associated deck</span></li>\n</ul><p><span>​</span></p><p><span>The Matriarch's flip condition is \"when the villain trash is shuffled into the villain deck\" flip her.</span></p><p><span>An incapacitated TLT, the nemesis of the Matriarch, can cause her to flip at will. If that was not planned it's an amazing coincidence, if it was, that's a whole new level of design to respect.</span></p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:46.231Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 3,
