      "raw": "<p>So last night we played a game via G+ against the Matriarch, we didn&#39;t win, despite our valiant attempt but we did learn an interesting thing.</p><p>Team Leader Tachyon&#39;s incapacitated powers are</p><ul><li>One Player draws 1 card now</li><li><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">One Player plays 1 card now</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Shuffle a trash into its associated deck</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">​</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">The Matriarch&#39;s flip condition is &quot;when the villain trash is shuffled into the villain deck&quot; flip her.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">An incapacitated TLT, the nemesis of the Matriarch, can cause her to flip at will. If that was not planned it&#39;s an amazing coincidence, if it was, that&#39;s a whole new level of design to respect.</span></p>",
